Selected MM backport host checks
===============================
Run from any directory with Python 3 and a host C compiler:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py --cc clang

HOSTCC is also supported (default cc). A compiler command can contain flags:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py \
    --cc 'clang -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all'

The runner compiles a temporary C program with production functions inserted
from the current tree: read_pages, swap_readpage, compaction predicates and
should_compact_retry, compaction trace feedback, do_shrink_slab and
quiet_vmstat. Filemap testing extracts only its two new callback guard blocks,
not the complete generic_file_buffered_read/filemap_fault implementations.
Use --source-root PATH to test another source tree with these changes.

Coverage:
* 36 filemap guard cases: absent callbacks, EIO, truncated-page passthrough,
  uptodate/error outcomes, callback-owned unlock and guarded unlock.
* 792 readahead cases: null mapping/a_ops, missing readpage, readpages
  preference, partial bulk-list consumption, callback errors, zero/1..32 pages,
  insertion failure, page-reference cleanup and plug balance.
* 160 swap cases: five routes (frontswap, swap file, block read_page, BIO
  allocation failure, completed BIO), workingset/cold, nested/non-nested,
  PSI disabled, synchronous/asynchronous and PageWorkingset changes during IO.
* 3,456 compaction retry combinations plus trace feedback and repeated
  withdrawn attempts: priorities, results, costly/non-costly/order0, LMK gate,
  suitability and retry counters. No-progress withdrawn retries must escalate
  or stop, while skipped/reclaim-needed retries retain their distinct logic.
* 11,440 shrinker cases: zero/positive seeks, priority, freeable counts,
  deferred work, direct/background batching and SHRINK_STOP.
* 12 quiet_vmstat outcomes and source guards for integrated zero-seek users,
  MGLRU shadow limits/classification and unchanged policy defaults.

Assertions remain enabled with NDEBUG. Wsign-compare/unused-parameter are
suppressed for kernel production code/mocks; other Wall/Wextra warnings fail.

Negative controls: EACH command must compile, then fail a C assertion:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py --negative donor-psi
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py --negative old-trace
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py --negative old-retry
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/mm_backport/test_backport.py --negative old-shrinker

Add --cc clang (or HOSTCC) as needed. A compile error is NOT a successful
negative control. The flags mutate the extracted test copy, never the tree.

Mocks are single-threaded and do not test real PSI/runqueue accounting,
concurrent page/callback lifetime changes, complete VFS faults/short reads,
allocator locks, real asynchronous IO, memcg/NUMA placement or shrinker races.
Shrinker tests model scan/deferred arithmetic, not actual memory reclaimed.
Source guards are not runtime proofs. No module or device-side test interface
is installed. See Documentation/vm/mm-selected-backports.rst for provenance,
corrections, build matrix and the remaining device-validation requirements.
